        <!-- ============ caption ============ -->
        <mxCell id="cap" value="Fig. 1. Overall architecture of GAST (Gap-Aware Spatio-Temporal forecaster). (a) The gap-aware evidence encoder converts the incomplete history into actor encodings H: an observation-evidence state (eligibility, age, reliability ρ_t = exp(−τ·Δ_t), learnable τ) drives the GERE spatial stage (per-frame agent attention with relational-geometry bias) and the ECTA temporal stage, which contains RMCM (reliability-modulated causal Mamba ×4) and EWSA (evidence-weighted state aggregation). (b) The future distribution decoder couples decoupled temporal state queries and 20 learnable mode queries (anchored at the focal agent) through state-consistency, mode-localization and hybrid-coupling modules, yielding 20 trajectory modes with probabilities and Laplace scales." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontColor=#202124;fontFamily=Times New Roman;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="742" width="1060" height="40" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

